From 4b3f950353d066ca02072fbf26d58b55f880b050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bugcheck <bugcheck@local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:07:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cars: near / far LOD meshes without holes or black smears
 (re-bake car LODs)

Yasin 7 Nov: lots of cars have black empty parts. Renders of all 12 models (original /
quarter / far): the quarter mesh (drawn up to 35 m) smeared dark grille / trim texels over the
bonnet and warped panels; the far mesh (35-140 m, most traffic and parked cars) from decimate()
(welded positions + meshoptimizer to 8 %) had holes, black torn panels and no wheels.
Both now come from Godot's import LOD generator (ImporterMesh.generate_lods: attribute-aware,
uv seams / normals / borders kept), never below the target count: quarter = the ~50 % level,
far = body and each wheel simplified separately to the ~20 % level, then merged. Far meshes
2.4k-4.4k triangles (were ~0.5k-1.4k, torn); MultiMesh draws, so no extra draw calls.
red_bake_car_lods.gd uses build_lods() for the far mesh; test_pb_carlods rebuilds it the same
way. Needs a car LOD re-bake (tools/red_bake_car_lods.gd, incremental: car LOD files only).
test_pb_carlods (FAIL on the release -> PASS), test_pb_carlods3, test_car_mesh PASS.
